=== p2-windows · W7 · page:system/DataExport (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:system/DataExport   kind=page   web route=/data-export
Web source  : web/src/features/system/pages/DataExportPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs + <Name>.Projection.cs (pure,
  Microsoft.UI-free projection, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (generated-client feed, ADR-004),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable observable state holder — the established testable
  pattern, see ExportsPageViewModel) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's idealized
  "DataExportPage.xaml + DataExportPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/System" is mapped onto these real
  conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("DataExport").
- Namespace: the page lives in TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.SystemOps (NOT ".System" — a ".System" leaf shadows the
  global System namespace and breaks every sibling feature-view's System.* references; CS0234). RouteTable already
  maps Page("DataExport","data-export",RouteGroup.SystemOps,"Data Export","\uEDE1"), so the route name is exact.
- Data sources bound to the generated C# client (ADR-004) through the DataExportClientFeed in DataExportPage.Source.cs:
  useCreateAccountExport -> POST /export/jobs/account (post_api_v1_export_jobs_account),
  useExportColumns        -> GET  /exports/columns?type= (get_api_v1_exports_columns),
  plus the export-jobs history (get_api_v1_export_jobs), vehicles (get_api_v1_vehicles) and the generic submit
  (post_api_v1_export_jobs) the page composes to render every panel. The default EmptyDataExportFeed resolves the
  empty state (the shell uses the parameterless ctor); the view-model is exercised in tests with a FakeDataExportFeed
  driving the loading/empty/error/success matrix.
- SI: the page carries no unit-bearing render fields beyond byte sizes (binary KB/MB/GB, web formatBytes) and
  ms durations (web formatDurationMsLong); both formatters are ported 1:1 in DataExportRegistration. Counts flow
  through the shared NumberFormatting port; timestamps through DateTimeFormatting (Full / Relative variants).
- Strings: 37 dataExport.* keys already existed verbatim in Strings/en/Resources.resw. The 11 bare manifest keys
  (All Vehicles, By Count, Export Failed[, Msg], Export Started[, Msg], Last Export, Most Exported, Start Export,
  Total Exports, Total Size) were absent from the windows catalog (the web renders them via i18next key-fallback,
  no default arg), so they were added as translation.<key>=<key> rows in ordinal-sorted position (XML re-validated,
  8235 -> 8246 data rows). Every C# call site passes the exact web key + English fallback through ILocalizer, so the
  page renders correct English even where the resw lookup misses.

